year’s freedom under such exceptional circumstances would have opened
up a prospect of unbounded bliss, the security of an irresponsible
existence. but harold was not like most boys. he had entertained, it
seems probable, some vague expectation that he would be invited to
remain.

it was, therefore, a very dazed young man who fairly tottered down the
