  there are, i have discovered, and i insert the discovery
  parenthetically for what it may be worth, two kinds of people in this
  world, those who long to be understood, and those who long to be
  misunderstood. it is the irony of life that neither is gratified.

  i am perfectly frank with you, dear laura, always; there seems to
  be no other reason for writing long letters. you know that i seek
  my thrills in a curious, vicarious way. you know that what befalls
