date. at first too modern, they soon grow old-fashioned. the very group
that is most enthusiastic about ulysses today will be the first to
spurn it tomorrow.

she lit another cigarette, reflecting on the words of clive bell, who
had said that in the best work of nicolas poussin the human figure is
treated as a shape cut out of coloured paper to be pinned on as the
composition directs. that was the right way to treat the human figure;
the mistake lay in making these shapes retain the characteristic
