general and her own participation in it in particular that it also
occurred to her that she might go so far as to do something for cupid.
she infrequently dined at a public restaurant, more seldom still did
she attend the theatre. it pleased cupid to do these things, which
to her were merely dull. her imagination supplied her with so much
better material than such casual experiences could give her. more and
